  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThis recipe is based on my personal photographic style, which emphasizes green tones, red tones, and beautiful skin tones. It delivers the soft, gentle gradation you’d find in film, featuring lush, deep greens and solid, confident reds. With a touch of magenta added to the highlights, it works wonderfully in both tree-filled parks and urban scenes where red elements frequently appear. The recipe truly comes alive in backlit situations — it’s perfect whenever you want to render skin tones in a bright, soft, and radiant way.",
